      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For the single-factor screening, the simple correlations with default_flag were all very small, so correlation alone was not useful for selecting variables. The AUC results were much more informative, and following the Module 2.2 rule, I kept factors with AUCs below 0.30 or above 0.65, which left 9 candidate factors for the multi-factor search.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "For the one-factor through four-factor models, performance improved steadily as more factors were added. The best one-factor model used asset_growth with a validation AUC of 0.7104, while the best four-factor model used net_profit_margin, asset_growth, rsch_devel_toa, and debt_value_toa, with the highest validation AUC of 0.8155 and test AUC of 0.9119. This suggests that adding profitability, growth, R&D intensity, and leverage information materially improved model discrimination.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "Among the one-factor to four-factor specifications, I would choose the four-factor model because it produced the strongest validation AUC and also the highest test AUC, with no obvious sign of performance deterioration."
      ],
